From: RetroArch-PI
Subject: [PATCH] new_dynarec arm64: remove the stray brk from fp_exception_ds

fp_exception_ds raises the Coprocessor Unusable exception for an FPU
instruction in a branch delay slot while Status.CU1 is clear. The ARM64
port starts it with a "brk 0" left in front of a complete body, which is
the same as the 32-bit ARM one (linkage_arm.S). Any game that does lazy
FPU switching with an FPU op in a delay slot dies with SIGTRAP: GoldenEye
007 and Perfect Dark, about 2 s after "Init new dynarec".

Without the brk both run on the dynarec at 97-100% (Orange Pi Zero3, H618
@ 1512 MHz). Replaces the earlier workaround that ran these two games on
the cached interpreter.

---
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/r4300/new_dynarec/arm64/linkage_aarch64.S
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/r4300/new_dynarec/arm64/linkage_aarch64.S
@@ -448,7 +448,6 @@
     br     x0
     
 GLOBAL_FUNCTION(fp_exception_ds):
-    brk    0
     mov    w2, #0x90000000 /* Set high bit if delay slot */
     b      .F1
     
